  "label": "User projected onto the man in the KKK robe as the speaker of the hateful text",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'man_in_kkk_robe' because the meme uses the man's attire and persona as the direct embodiment of the hateful message in the text. The text 'i hate when i see a black out in my neighborhood' and 'but i still offer my neighbors a candle' is presented as if spoken by the man in the robe, making the user identify with or project themselves onto this hateful speaker. The visual material of the man in the KKK robe is the focal point onto which the user's perspective is projected, as the meme's intent is to make the viewer see themselves as the agent of the racist sentiment.",
